<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/inventions?focus=printing-press">Inventions &amp; Discoveries</a> · Writing and counting</p><h1 class="enc-title">Printing press</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as printing</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Printing is the mechanical reproduction of text and images. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/woodblock-printing">Woodblock printing</a> developed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang Dynasty</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bi-sheng">Bi Sheng</a> invented <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/movable-type">movable type</a> around 1040 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>, with printing spreading further under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan Dynasty</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg">Gutenberg</a>'s printing press, developed in the fifteenth century in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>, helped spread learning and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/printing-press.jpg" alt="Printing press" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: International Printing Museum · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gutenberg_press.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="inv-entry"><h2 class="enc-section-title">On the inventions tree</h2><dl class="inv-entry-facts"><div><dt>First known</dt><dd>c. 1440</dd></div><div><dt>Where</dt><dd>Mainz</dd></div><div><dt>Credited to</dt><dd><a href="/encyclopedia/johannes-gutenberg">Johannes Gutenberg</a> · <a href="/empire/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a></dd></div></dl><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Built on</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/papermaking">Papermaking<span>179–141 BCE</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/movable-type">Movable type<span>c. 1040</span></a></div><div class="inv-entry-rel"><span class="inv-k">Led to</span><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/de-humani-corporis-fabrica">Modern anatomy<span>1543</span></a><a class="inv-chip" href="/encyclopedia/newspaper">Newspaper<span>1605</span></a></div><p class="enc-article-foot"><a class="enc-random-link" href="/inventions?focus=printing-press">See it on the inventions tree &rarr;</a></p></section>
